// `def` binds a name for later items to use.
//
// The session runs a definition's body once, at definition time, and stores
// the returned *value* -- later expressions see that value, never a re-run of
// the computation (the memoization a REPL user expects, and a first taste of
// CBPV's explicit sequencing: things run exactly where the program says they
// run).
// (The `;` matters: newlines are insignificant between items, so a value
// definition is terminated explicitly -- otherwise the next item would be
// read as a continuation of this expression.)
def greeting = "the value zone";

// A variable is a value (CBPV: only values can be variables), so returning it
// is again one `ret` away.
ret greeting

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: greeting
//@ expect-last-value: "the value zone"
